+# FIX-124 — Live protection deadlock recovery and input isolation
 
-Status: PLANNED — TO BE DONE. No wallet transaction/locking code changed.
+Status: CANDIDATE IMPLEMENTED; Maven/JUnit and MySQL validation pending. The broader deadlock investigation remains open. This is not a claim that all wallet deadlocks are eliminated.
 
-The team reports nine wallet_managed_position deadlock incidents. Those incidents have not been independently verified here. Obtain actual deadlock/transaction evidence, reproduce the cause and design one scoped repair with concurrency, rollback and recovery tests.
+## Evidence and project identity
 
-A possible synchronized-method/transaction-commit visibility gap was identified during FIX-122 review but not reproduced. Do not call it the deadlock cause without evidence. Transaction coordination for this possible race is now reserved separately as FIX-125. FIX-122 uses read-only committed history and a price-stage recheck; it does not claim to repair wallet serialization.
+Project crypto-ai-trader; database crypto_ai; log C:\apps\crypto-ai\crypto-ai.log.
+On 2026-09-08 the trader log records deadlocks at 01:55:05 (PEPE candle analysis), 07:41:05 (UNI live protection), 09:15:34 (BNB recovery), and 09:33:02 (BNB live protection), all UTC+02:00. The complete UNI stack places failure at LivePositionProtectionService's first managed-position locking lookup. BinanceKlineService catches the exception but its surrounding transaction subsequently throws UnexpectedRollbackException at commit. This confirms a protection failure can invalidate writes sharing the kline transaction.
+
+The separately supplied InnoDB latest-deadlock report names crypto_ai_v2, the crypto-ai-next database. Its lock cycle is NOT treated as proof of trader's root cause. The trader lookup index (symbol,status,opened_at) already exists.
+
+## Candidate change and explicit behavioral effects
+
+BinanceKlineService now requires no ambient transaction. KlineTransactionCoordinator performs sequential independent transactions:
+
+1. Persist the candle and, for the canonical 1m stream, its exact price observation together; commit before acquiring any position lock.
+2. Evaluate the existing live-protection business logic in a fresh transaction. Only a MySQL 1213/40001 thrown by the FIRST managed-position lookup receives a retry marker. After rollback, allow one immediate retry (two attempts total). No retry of later decision, wallet, observer or ambiguous commit failures.
+3. Persist a RECOVERED or FAILED incident for a retried/failed evaluation in a separate bounded transaction. A normal tick creates no diagnostic row. RECOVERED means evaluation committed, not necessarily that a SELL executed.
+4. Run the existing debug observer independently. Its rollback cannot undo input or protection.
+5. Publish a closed-candle event inside a new transaction after protection finishes, retaining the existing AFTER_COMMIT listener and protection-before-dispatch ordering.
+
+An exhausted or nonretryable protection failure retains the input and allows closed-candle dispatch; the incident remains visible. If input persistence itself fails, protection and dispatch are not invoked. This intentionally prevents protection from consuming an input that failed to persist. No delayed background replay of failed price ticks is introduced.
+
+These are Production transaction/recovery changes. A previously failed initial check can now succeed, so actual executions can differ during contention. Input becomes visible to other database readers earlier, and a protection commit is retained even if the later observer or dispatch fails. The split no longer provides one all-or-nothing kline/protection transaction. A process crash after input commit but before protection/dispatch can leave committed input without that evaluation; durable exactly-once tick processing is not introduced by this patch. No score, threshold, sizing, exit formula, price fallback or wallet authority is changed. Exact symbol + interval + candle_open_time lineage and Binance observed time remain intact.
+
+## Observability and Replay
+
+Search [FIX-124][PRODUCTION][INITIAL_LOCK_RETRY], [RECOVERED], [FAILED], [OBSERVER_FAILED], and [DIAGNOSTIC_PERSIST_FAILED]. The latter reports inability to persist diagnostics; it does not undo committed work.
+V84 creates fix124_protection_incident with original candle/observation identity, price, attempts, outcome and failure text. No foreign-key lock on the managed position is added. Queries are indexed by symbol/observed_at.
+Proven / Analyze Trades displays Production incidents for active/archived Replay windows and a saved trade's own entry/exit window, explicitly labelled as Production history rather than simulated outcomes. This is a live query of durable history, not a frozen saved snapshot. No rows means no recorded incidents in that window, not proof that all checks succeeded. Historical incidents before this migration are not fabricated. Results are limited to 500 and truncation is disclosed.
+Replay's simulated business logic and OLD/NEW data paths are unchanged. Replay never reads the incident table as a decision input. Retry mechanics are not copied into a single-threaded simulated wallet. No historical parity or timing result is claimed.
+
+## Tests and validation
+
+Added Maven/JUnit tests using H2 JDBC transactions to reproduce the old catch-and-continue rollback symptom, and verify new input retention, rollback before retry, bounded exhaustion, no late-failure retry, observer isolation, input-failure suppression, diagnostic failure isolation, first-lock-only marking, exact observation persistence and protection-before-close commit ordering. Controlled exceptions model the reported failure point; they do NOT reproduce the unidentified MySQL competing transaction.
+
+Actual authoring checks: 11 Node tests passed, zero failures. Java syntax parsing and JS syntax checks recorded in DELIVERY-FIX-124-126.md. `mvn -f fix124-126/pom.xml test` could not start: command not found (exit 127). Maven/JUnit tests have NOT passed or run here. Environment provides Java 17; project requires Java 21. No MySQL migration, full application compile, live concurrency or historical Replay comparison was run.
+
+Before deployment: run Maven under Java 21; validate V84/V85 on a copy of crypto_ai; exercise real Spring/JPA concurrent protection and analysis with MySQL; compare representative Replay windows. Keep the exact trader deadlock cycle and PEPE/BNB analysis/recovery failures OPEN until reproduced and verified. This patch handles the identified live-protection failure boundary, not every analysis/transaction path.
+
+## Separate work
+
+FIX-123 sizing remains planned. FIX-125 synchronization through wallet commit remains planned and unimplemented. FIX-126 addresses audit-message capacity separately. No synchronized wallet BUY/SELL method or wallet transaction coordinator is changed by this candidate.
